<title>USA: Fujitsu unit cuts tablet PC price 34 pct.</title>
<headline>Fujitsu unit cuts tablet PC price 34 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SANTA CLARA, Calif. 1996-09-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Fujitsu Personal Systems Inc, a U.S. unit of electronics manufacturer Fujitsu Ltd, said it is cutting 34 percent from the price of its tablet PC, the Stylistic 500.</p>
<p>Now priced at $1,995 the Stylistic 500 has a 50-megahertz, 486 microprocessor, four megabytes of dynamic random access memorty a 170-megabyte hard drive and 8-inch display. It has a pen-based interface and uses Windows software.</p>
<p>The Stylistic 500's target market includes companies deploying a mobile work force using complex computing.</p>
</text>
